Now UI combo. Rewrite comboHit/updateCombo/setCombo in ui.js to keep text/rank in sync and avoid the stale 0. Need rank helper. Also avoid timeout hide conflicting with continuous timer.

Implementation:
```js
rankFor(count) { ... }

comboHit(count, timerRatio) {
  if (count <= 0) { this.setCombo(0,0); return; }
  this.comboRender(count, timerRatio);
  this.el.comboDisplay.classList.add('show');
}

updateCombo(count, timerRatio) {
  if (count <= 0) { this.setCombo(0,0); return; }
  this.comboRender(count, timerRatio);
  this.el.comboDisplay.classList.add('show');
}

comboRender(count, timerRatio) {
  if (this.comboLast !== count) {
    this.comboLast = count;
    this.el.comboCount.textContent = String(count);
    this.el.comboRank.textContent = rankFor(count);
  }
  this.el.comboTimer.style.transform = ...
}
setCombo(count, timerRatio=0) {
  if (count <=0) {
    if (this.comboLast !== 0) {
      this.comboLast = 0;
      this.el.comboCount.textContent = '0';
      this.el.comboRank.textContent = 'EN RACHA';
    }
    this.el.comboDisplay.classList.remove('show');
    return;
  }
  ...
}
```
Remove comboHideTimer / setTimeout: Keep updateComboUi driving show. But when player stops, updateComboUi must hide. In Game.updateComboUi call setCombo(0) when combo<=0. However, updateComboUi runs every frame after player.update; player.update may have set combo to 0 and called setCombo already. Fine.

Need to ensure when UI initially has comboDisplay class hidden? HTML has no show. Good.

Also combo count "0" while hidden not visible anyway. But fix displayed count.

Now Game.updateComboUi: add else setCombo(0,0). Also alert show only while timer >0. Let's do.

