Now HUD stat labels. Improve desktop. We can use `.stat { min-width: 108px; padding: 0 18px; }` and `.stat-label { font-size: 8px; letter-spacing: .18em; white-space: nowrap; }`. Maybe current is okay; summary says crowding. Let's adjust to .19em and min-width 104. Also the run-stats has no max. Fine.

Wall visuals: add chevrons in scene drawWalls. Let's implement before graffiti, perhaps after rails:

```js
this.drawWallChevrons(ctx, left, groundY, 'left', this.wallPulse.left);
this.drawWallChevrons(ctx, right, groundY, 'right', this.wallPulse.right);
```

Function draws stacked inward-pointing chevrons from y groundY-30 to groundY-210, with alpha pulsing and last hits glow. Use direction. Also draw dashed vertical guide.

Implementation:
```js
drawWallChevrons(ctx, x, groundY, side, pulseAmount) {
  const dir = side === 'left' ? 1 : -1;
  ctx.save();
  ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(140,250,255,.28)';
  ctx.lineWidth = 1;
  ctx.setLineDash([3,7]);
  ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + dir*6, groundY-24); ctx.lineTo(x + dir*6, groundY-230); ctx.stroke();
  ctx.setLineDash([]);
  const base = 0.18 + pulseAmount*0.6;
  for (let i=0;i<4;i++){
    const y = groundY - 34 - i*46;
    const alpha = base * (1 - i*0.13) * (0.7 + 0.3*Math.sin(this.time*2.2 + i));
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(140,250,255,${clamp(alpha,0,1)})`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.shadowColor='#39f5ff'; ctx.shadowBlur=6+pulseAmount*10;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + dir*5, y - 7);
    ctx.lineTo(x + dir*17, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + dir*5, y + 7);
    ctx.stroke();
  }
  ctx.restore();
}
```
Also maybe a "WALL JUMP" label along wall. Existing NO EXIT at -115. Could replace left graffiti with 'MURO · SALTO' and right 'WALL JUMP'. But that's part of discoverability. Let's change left text to 'SALTO DE MURO' and right to 'WALL JUMP · SALTO'. Maybe better: left "SALTO DE PARED" rotated; right "WALL JUMP". That indicates mechanic. Let's do.

Also barrier base alpha increase from .06 to .1 and rails. Fine.

